@@ -8,19 +8,30 @@ npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH cha
 npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["home"] }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones; `?tag=home` keeps the tasks with that tag (the filters combine) | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "tags": ["home"] }` (`tags` is optional) | 201, the task, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title`, `done` and / or `tags` (which replaces the whole list; without `tags` they stay as they are) | 200, the task, 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` (nothing changes), or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
+| `GET /api/tags` | Lists the tags in use with their number of tasks, sorted by name: `[{ "name": "home", "count": 2 }]` | 200, an array |
+
+### Tags
+
+A task's `tags` is an array of strings sorted alphabetically, `[]` by default. Tags are normalized (trimmed, lowercased,
+duplicates removed), then each must be 1 to 30 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `-`, and a task has at most 10;
+otherwise the request answers 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }`. A tag that no task uses any more disappears from
+`GET /api/tags`. They are stored in the `tags` and `task_tags` tables; deleting a task removes its links.
+
+On the page, each task shows its tags: click one to show only the tasks with that tag, and use "Show all tags" to come
+back. The add form takes comma-separated tags.
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
 
